"text": ""
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 240),
"speaker": "Duke"
},
&"1_74": {
"dialogue": "Hark! An excellent job indeed!",
"offset": Vector2(-2400, 2800),
"options": {
0: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"1_33",
"text": ""
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 240),
"speaker": "Duke"
},
&"1_75": {
"dialogue": "Do you know what the difference between your [i]Primary[/i] and [i]Secondary[/i] types?",
"offset": Vector2(-740, 1280),
"options": {
0: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"1_77",
"text": "Yes"
},
1: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"1_91",
"text": "No"
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 308),
"speaker": 2
},
&"1_77": {
"dialogue": "Right, so unlike your [i]Secondary[/i] type, your [i]Primary[/i] type changes rather infrequently.",
"offset": Vector2(-420, 1280),
"options": {
0: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"1_78",
"text": ""
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 240),
"speaker": 2
},
&"1_78": {
"dialogue": "Its usually after a battle has ended. I think it probably has something to do with your adrenaline... anyway, that's not important.",
"offset": Vector2(-100, 1280),
"options": {
0: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"1_79",
"text": ""
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 240),
"speaker": 2
},
&"1_79": {
"dialogue": "Every time this happens the elemental changes will permeate deeper into your core.",
"offset": Vector2(220, 1280),
"options": {
0: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"1_80",
"text": ""
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 240),
"speaker": 2
},
&"1_8": {
"dialogue": ".....",
"offset": Vector2(-3400, 520),
"options": {
0: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"5_3",
"text": ""
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 240),
"speaker": "Monster"
},
&"1_80": {
"dialogue": "Until one day, probably a year or two from now, when the changes fully reach your center. This is called [i]alignment[/i] (or bias by old timers).",
"offset": Vector2(540, 1280),
"options": {
0: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"1_81",
"text": ""
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 240),
"speaker": 2
},
&"1_81": {
"dialogue": "Once you're aligned to a particular element, your [i]Primary[/i] type will be locked and then the real changes begin...",
"offset": Vector2(860, 1280),
"options": {
0: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"1_82",
"text": ""
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 240),
"speaker": 2
},
&"1_82": {
"dialogue": "[el]Blue[/el] alignment is fairly simple. You've actually already seen the breadth of this condition. Everyone in this room is [el]Blue[/el]-aligned, besides you two of course. I'm still pretty early in the transformation, the poker players are about halfway through, and the fitness guys are pretty late stage. And to finally answer your question, one of the first symptoms of [el]Blue[/el]-alignment is growing roots, which really limits your mobility.",
"offset": Vector2(1180, 1280),
"options": {
0: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"1_83",
"text": "That sounds scary..."
},
1: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"1_86",
"text": "What about the other elements?"
},
2: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([{
"operator": 0,
"value1": "met_mini_boss",
"value2": "yes"
}]),
"link": &"1_87",
"text": "Is the monster out there also Blue-aligned?"
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 343),
"speaker": 2
},
&"1_83": {
"dialogue": "Yeah, everyone thinks so at first... Its one of those facts of life you kinda just have to accept.",
"offset": Vector2(1500, 1280),
"options": {
0: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"1_84",
"text": ""
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 240),
"speaker": 2
},
&"1_84": {
"dialogue": "Plus, more times than not you'll find one element you just click with and that lessens the existential horror of it.",
"offset": Vector2(1820, 1320),
"options": {
0: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": &"1_85",
"text": ""
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 240),
"speaker": 2
},
&"1_85": {
"dialogue": "But until then its better to just not think about it too hard.",
"offset": Vector2(2140, 1320),
"options": {
0: {
"condition": Array[Dictionary]([]),
"link": "END",
"text": ""
}
},
"size": Vector2(300, 240),
"speaker": 2
},
&"1_86": {
"dialogue": "To be honest, I don't really remember or know much about them. One symptom of [el]Blue[/el]-alignment is that you trade your understanding of the other elements for a deeper connection to [el]Blue[/el].",
"offset": Vector2(1560, 1580),
"options": {
0: {
